{"event_type":"review","id":"9af185aa04befb77019502b27c367c43c9a39f83e613b4e157997d56584b306b","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T17:03:44Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/29c1304f7a7fc0361130f5814c6d9a5541d832fc304c3616905945b2eb92970a","sha256":"29c1304f7a7fc0361130f5814c6d9a5541d832fc304c3616905945b2eb92970a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/db7a451ceb0e901274e387f9cb309a3c92910b5c1b1fde1a7f7de01f0cc96a49","sha256":"db7a451ceb0e901274e387f9cb309a3c92910b5c1b1fde1a7f7de01f0cc96a49"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/592ef2dfe8e05ab13ea827f058158e1e80b6e5f45c58b7ca1a9778f0dabc0aa9","sha256":"592ef2dfe8e05ab13ea827f058158e1e80b6e5f45c58b7ca1a9778f0dabc0aa9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c6f1fe913d63a30fb011e5d7a6fc36c1445f59035ef50f2c7e07dcceffbfecd7","sha256":"c6f1fe913d63a30fb011e5d7a6fc36c1445f59035ef50f2c7e07dcceffbfecd7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e74681082f942489ae23c6abb673af0a7f84f3e1944896566494313c106fac0b","sha256":"e74681082f942489ae23c6abb673af0a7f84f3e1944896566494313c106fac0b"}],"attempt_id":"420e2cfc77559d57a7c9590a8d83355633a338db3942d0c11daada6f60a00edc:0:1","base":"3559fca6030f7dc54c5a615b2d92ec46ee02a523","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d80da77e3fb5b1696766a8512f138f9efb2ad85f","body":"**`--json` mode writes `CQ_*` env warnings to stderr. This breaks the I1 empty-stderr contract.**\n\n`src/cli/main.ts:538` writes every `check.warningLines` entry to `io.stderr` and does not check the mode. The comment at `src/cli/main.ts:515-518` says this is intentional in `--json` mode. Two contracts disagree with it:\n\n- `policy/DOCTRINE.md` I1 says: \"In machine mode (`--json`) stderr stays empty.\"\n- `src/cli/README.md:31-33` says `--json` \"suppresses narration entirely (machine mode): stderr stays empty on every path\".\n\nTrigger: an unknown or reserved `CQ_*` variable in the environment, plus any `--json` invocation other than `config`. Result: stderr is not empty, so a CI gate that treats non-empty stderr as a protocol breach rejects a clean run. The error branch above already uses `rawMode` to keep machine mode quiet. The warning branch does not.\n\nGate the warning loop on the mode. Do not narrate warnings in machine mode. If the warnings must reach the operator, add a contract slot for them. If the stderr exception is deliberate, update the doctrine and the README. Do not leave code and contract in disagreement.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    for (const line of check.warningLines) io.stderr(`${line}\\n`);\n+    // I1: machine mode keeps stderr empty on every path.\n+    if (rawMode !== 'json') {\n+      for (const line of check.warningLines) io.stderr(`${line}\\n`);\n+    }\n```\n\nAlso update the comment at lines 515-518 to match.\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines: \"In machine mode (`--json`) stderr stays empty and an error that has no result writes one … object to stdout instead\". As per path instructions: \"stdout carries exactly one JSON artifact per invocation…; stderr is cq:-prefixed narration\".","id":"a9196bc427f470c9f628cd1bdd685a670a8bae717daeecdd0353b744bf35a20b","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`--json` mode writes `CQ` env warnings to stderr. This breaks the I1 empty-stderr contract."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"295ef75f9077f9241b260bc61f6b9464a258f257","body":"**Serialize removal with the append chain.**\n\nIf a caller starts `remove` while an append is pending on the same `SessionStore`, `rm` can run after the existence check. The append can then recreate a headerless file, which `load` cannot read.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Queue removal on the write chain</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    await Promise.all([\n-      rm(this.pathFor(sessionId), { force: true }),\n-      rm(join(this.sessionsDir, `${sessionId}.cq-cli-session`), { force: true }),\n-    ]);\n+    const remove = async (): Promise<void> => {\n+      await Promise.all([\n+        rm(this.pathFor(sessionId), { force: true }),\n+        rm(join(this.sessionsDir, `${sessionId}.cq-cli-session`), { force: true }),\n+      ]);\n+    };\n+    const next = this.tail.then(remove, remove);\n+    this.tail = next.catch(() => undefined);\n+    await next;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"b25e91bc93467e478b2953be3d4f4c8f2cec6d706a3aa80b4dd804050a8dedad","intervals":[],"path":"src/harness/session.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Serialize removal with the append chain."}],"head":"ae9d8811a88527efedd1184ea5ab7bbd97f6f6a1","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"8c416254b6029a57f689760a39116bcc6c5edff5","intervals":[[1,224]],"path":".oxlintrc.json"},{"blob":"18c597e52e4f1544f754c0970be2f3d528a1bdf7","intervals":[[10,13],[38,42],[46,50],[54,60],[151,152]],"path":"docs/dd-2-usd-normalization.md"},{"blob":"c3c61f9f957db1383fbd46efff8311e4e08994e9","intervals":[[36,36],[47,53],[56,58],[60,61],[77,80],[98,101],[125,126],[128,131],[134,137],[153,159]],"path":"docs/dd-9-api-equivalent-budget.md"},{"blob":"8dfc46a5783e86702da209dbd413195ee8795cc1","intervals":[[5,5],[8,30],[32,44],[47,52],[54,54],[56,63],[69,70]],"path":"src/cli/README.md"},{"blob":"d80da77e3fb5b1696766a8512f138f9efb2ad85f","intervals":[[16,31],[39,40],[44,50],[54,63],[65,67],[70,70],[72,76],[79,83],[88,91],[93,94],[96,96],[103,103],[108,109],[111,114],[117,118],[143,162],[166,171],[177,183],[206,216],[224,229],[232,237],[246,249],[251,255],[261,262],[265,265],[297,297],[335,351],[355,355],[380,381],[391,393],[397,405],[419,422],[431,431],[440,460],[463,467],[482,495],[499,509],[513,541],[548,555],[558,565],[580,580],[582,584],[586,